3. Prior outreach and express authorization
Before undertaking an activity requiring permission, submit a licensing
request at:
https://github.com/giasonpooni/A-Man-of-Two-Worlds/issues/new?template=licensing-request.yml

A request begins discussion; it does not authorize use. Authorization
requires an express written grant signed by a duly authorized
representative of the actual rights holder, identifying the exact
material/version, licensee, permitted acts and purposes, deployment and
users, territory, term, fees if any, and any required conditions.
The grant must identify the legal licensor holding the relevant rights
and the signer's authority; group affiliation alone does not supply either.
No sublicensing, transfer, derivative-work rights, additional deployment,
or other rights arise beyond the signed grant's express scope.
If approved distribution or operation requires installation, execution,
necessary copies or output use, the signed grant must address those acts.
Do not put confidential assets or personal contact details in public issues.

